          "text": "60 positives out of 800. Write a script: stratified CV (e.g., 5-fold), pipeline StandardScaler+PCA(n) fit on train folds, compute reconstruction-based score? How to use PCA for fault discrimination? Common approach: use T² / SPE (residual) as anomaly score, compute AUC on test fold. Compare n=3,4,5. Actually simpler: project to n comps and train a classifier? The user said \"前處理和 PCA 只在訓練折擬合\", comparing AUC. Using T²/SPE monitoring statistic is natural for fault monitoring. I'll use SPE (residual) plus maybe T2. Let me do both, or use a score = T² of residual... Keep it simple: compute both T² and Q (SPE) statistics, AUC per statistic, average across folds. Report.",
